HOLyHammer
==========

HOLyHammer selects premises for a goal, translates the goal and premises to
TPTP, schedules time slices across external provers, and reconstructs a proof
with Metis.  It returns as soon as the first reconstructed proof is verified.

Usage
-----

At least one external prover must be installed.

    load "holyHammer";
    open holyHammer;
    hh ([], ``1 + 1 = 2``);
    holyhammer ``1 + 1 = 2``;

The overall default timeout is 30 seconds.  `set_timeout` is deprecated; use
the option interface instead:

    hhConfig.hh_set ("timeout", "60");
    hhConfig.hh_set ("provers", "e vampire");
    hhConfig.hh_params ();
    hhConfig.print_params ();

`hh_set` validates values immediately.  `hh_params` returns every effective
option as `(name, value, provenance)`, while `print_params` prints the same
information with short descriptions.  Runtime settings take precedence over
the user or system configuration and environment; use `hh_unset` to remove a
runtime override.

The options are `timeout`, `max_proofs`, `provers`, `slices`, `cores`,
`filter`, `max_facts`, `minimize`, `preplay_timeout`, `minimize_timeout`,
`cache`, `cache_dir`, `cache_max_entries`, and `debug_dir`.  Set `filter` to
`none` to use all available premises in dependency order.  The old public
references `timeout_glob`, `premise_selection_flag`, and `all_atps` have been
removed; their replacements are the `timeout`, `filter`, and `provers`
options.  `lemmas_glob` has also been removed: integrations should consume
`main_hh_lemmas` directly.

The scheduled prover names are `e`, `vampire`, and `zipperposition`.  The
`z3` registry entry remains callable through `hhProver`, but has no scheduler
slices.  The temporary Phase 0 `e-legacy` and `vampire-legacy` registry
entries have been removed.

Installing provers
------------------

The recommended installation command is:

    tools/download-provers

The fixed twelve-goal end-to-end smoke suite exercises E, Vampire, and
Zipperposition through export, proof search, and reconstruction:

    cd src/holyhammer
    ../../bin/Holmake smoke.exe
    ./smoke.exe

Alternatively, put a supported binary on `PATH`.  HOLyHammer looks for
`eprover-ho` or `eprover`, `vampire`, `zipperposition`, and, for the
schedule-less Z3 entry, `z3_tptp` or `z3`.

The tested versions are:

* E 3.2.5-ho ("Puttabong Moondrop");
* Vampire 5.0.1; and
* Zipperposition 2.1, Isabelle component revision 2.

Executable discovery
--------------------

A prover executable may also be selected in
`$HOME/.hol4/hammer/config` or `$HOLDIR/etc/hammer-config`:

    prover.e.executable = /opt/e/bin/eprover

User configuration takes precedence over system configuration.  Dedicated
environment variables are also supported:

* `HOL4_EPROVER_EXECUTABLE`;
* `HOL4_VAMPIRE_EXECUTABLE`;
* `HOL4_ZIPPERPOSITION_EXECUTABLE`; and
* `HOL4_Z3_EXECUTABLE`.

Discovery checks configuration, the dedicated environment variable, `PATH`,
and versioned installation directories under
`$HOLDIR/src/holyhammer/provers` and `$HOME/.hol4/hammer/provers`.

